1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,680
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:08,380
I was wrong.
I was going to return it.

5
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:10,750
I was on my way
to the police station.

6
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,950
There's still plenty of money left.

7
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:18,160
I made a mistake, sir.

8
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:19,790
Okay? Please spare me.

9
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:22,390
I was wrong. I was so wrong.

10
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:23,960
That's enough.

11
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,810
- Let's leave it at that.
- Who the heck are you?

12
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,210
Should I call the police?

13
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,090
Consider yourself lucky, punk.

14
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:52,520
- Let's go.
- Got it.

15
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,470
Are you okay?

16
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:06,370
What?

17
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,940
Yes...

18
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,350
That must've been a scare.

19
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:20,020
I'm someone who helps people...

20
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:21,950
like you, sir.

21
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:25,390
(Choi Jun Hwan, Social Worker,
Onnuri Homeless Support Center)

22
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:29,730
I see. You're a social worker.

23
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,370
Let's get you to a doctor first.

24
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:36,940
- This way.
- Right.

25
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,670
(Cheongma Food's
Premium Food Hall Proposal)

26
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:45,680
You want Cheongma Food to enter...

27
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:47,310
the Premium Food Hall?

28
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:49,850
The more detailed conditions...

29
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:51,980
are organized below.

30
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:56,290
An 18 percent commission?

31
00:01:57,820 --> 00:02:00,860
The premium food hall commission is
usually in the 20 percent range.

32
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:02,760
Are you aware of that?

33
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:05,530
Yes, of course. I know it very well.

34
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,270
You're trying to use my weakness...

35
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:09,570
to make one big score.

36
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,300
Come to think of it,

37
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,910
one big score might not be enough.

38
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,580
If you had just gracefully accepted
the tea set I offered,

39
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:24,920
none of this would be happening.

40
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,450
Do you think you can avoid
those shackles?

41
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:34,130
Even I, who know the true nature
of this industry to the bone,

42
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:37,600
didn't realize the ground
beneath my feet was rotting.

43
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,900
Since you don't have
any solid backing,

44
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,740
imagine how much worse it will get.

45
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,340
We'll just wait and see...

46
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:50,010
what kind of stench you'll give off
as you live.

47
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:57,950
I guarantee you,

48
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,650
it'll be far worse for you
than it ever was for me.

49
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,760
No, perhaps the ground
beneath your feet...

50
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,560
is already starting to rot.

51
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:12,030
For now, both my feet...

52
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,230
are perfectly fine.

53
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:15,830
Don't you get it?

54
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:18,040
You're different from us.

55
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,510
Your foundation is muddy
and soft ground,

56
00:03:22,010 --> 00:03:23,510
so how could anything not rot?

57
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,210
I'll accept this proposal.

58
00:03:28,350 --> 00:03:29,550
Enjoy your meal.

59
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:13,290
Here.
I got you some basic necessities.

60
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:18,500
Are you sure I can stay here?

61
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,700
Yes. If you need anything else,

62
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,430
reach out to me at the number
on my business card.

63
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,340
I guess I was really lucky today.

64
00:04:27,910 --> 00:04:30,480
I even got to meet my savior.

65
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:35,610
Oh, and for the time being,
you don't need to look for a job.

66
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,280
If you help organize supplies
and clean the motel,

67
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:42,150
they've agreed to pay you
a decent daily wage.

68
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,620
What? Really?

69
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:52,230
Does that mean
I'll have a steady income now?

70
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:59,270
Of course. As long as there are
no major issues while you stay here,

71
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:02,540
our center plans
to support you continuously.

72
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:04,710
An Guk Cheol,

73
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,510
your luck is finally turning around.

74
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,780
Thank you.

75
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,150
Wait, what should I call you?

76
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:17,760
Mr. Social Worker? Or sir?

77
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:19,820
Call me
whatever you're comfortable with.

78
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:22,890
Right, got it.
I'll call you Mr. Choi.

79
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:25,060
Thank you, Mr. Choi.

80
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,170
No way.

81
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:44,020
So this is where
you're holding An Guk Cheol?

82
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,580
Yes. I gave him
the motel cleaning job,

83
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:48,850
so he'll be staying in this area
for a while.

84
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,820
A leopard can't change its spots.

85
00:05:51,890 --> 00:05:55,030
He won't be able to stay away
from the gambling dens.

86
00:05:55,990 --> 00:05:58,300
I figured as much,
so I chose a motel...

87
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,930
surrounded by gambling dens
and adult arcades.

88
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:03,630
- Is that so?
- Also, he'll be paid daily...

89
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,570
instead of monthly.

90
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,970
That way, he'll gamble away
everything he earns right away.

91
00:06:09,810 --> 00:06:10,810
Good.

92
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,840
That will keep him
from getting any other ideas.

93
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:15,450
But keep him on a short leash.

94
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:18,450
Check in on him occasionally
so he doesn't try anything funny.

95
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:20,080
Yes, understood.

96
00:06:21,250 --> 00:06:22,420
Good work, Secretary Choi.

97
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:38,640
Do you think Ms. Kang
will come in today?

98
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,770
She took a day off for her hangover,

99
00:06:41,010 --> 00:06:42,570
so she'll probably show up today.

100
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,810
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

101
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,560
Nothing happened
while I was gone, right?

102
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:02,490
- No.
- No.

103
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,600
Ko Eun Seol.

104
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:19,980
You seem to be fine.

105
00:07:20,910 --> 00:07:22,050
As for me,

106
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:24,880
my stomach can't handle anything
other than premium whiskey or wine.

107
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,220
Drinking that cheap soju...

108
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:28,850
really threw me off my game.

109
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,230
How about a rematch,
this time with good whiskey or wine?

110
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:36,090
You sure love your alcohol,
don't you?

111
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:39,330
If you don't have any tasks for me,
I'll get back to work.

112
00:07:40,630 --> 00:07:43,000
Instead of focusing on drinking,
try focusing on your work.

113
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,010
This is the fabric inventory report
for this quarter...

114
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:50,640
and the unit price changes
by supplier.

115
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:53,880
Do a full review
and organize it for the new line.

116
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,020
I thought
the Planning Team handled this.

117
00:07:58,350 --> 00:08:00,150
How can
a designer create products...

118
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:01,750
without knowing
how the fabric market works?

119
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:05,790
Then shouldn't our side
just request the data from them?

120
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:09,960
You talk too much, Ko Eun Seol.

121
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:13,460
Since when is talking back
considered a skill?

122
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:16,770
Trying to act tough
just makes you look petty.

123
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:20,710
Am I really the only one?

124
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,150
She's making my blood boil again.

125
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,920
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

126
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:34,350
These days, even luxury brands use
OEMs in Southeast Asia and China...

127
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,990
to secure their margins.

128
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:39,160
But from fabric sourcing
to sewing and finishing,

129
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:41,560
you want to run everything
through domestic lines?

130
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,160
Chief Cha,

131
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,460
can we actually make
the numbers work?

132
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,700
I've determined
that financial viability...

133
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:51,570
doesn't come from simply cutting
immediate labor costs,

134
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:55,310
but from reducing
unnecessary opportunity costs.

135
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,910
If we boost the repeat purchase rate
through domestic production...

136
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,210
and eliminate
unnecessary defect losses,

137
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:02,910
our net margin
will look quite strong.

138
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,880
Truly a master of words, aren't you?

139
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,790
But you know, business...

140
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:11,690
doesn't run on such slick words.

141
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,060
Anyway, let's wait and see.

142
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:19,060
Will the margins actually justify
skipping overseas sourcing?

143
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,430
That reminds me.

144
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:27,610
I hear you're attending
Director Min's whiskey launch event.

145
00:09:28,310 --> 00:09:30,070
I plan to go with Ms. Kang.

146
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:32,940
Chief Cha, is that really necessary?

147
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:39,420
You and Director Min went
to high school together, right?

148
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,050
Yes, we were in the same class.

149
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:45,060
Then I suppose you can attend.

150
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:48,560
But you know, friendships...

151
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:51,600
can sometimes become
an unnecessary obstacle in society.

152
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:54,270
Sometimes they are just a burden.

153
00:09:55,530 --> 00:09:56,530
I see.

154
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,170
Anyway, understood.

155
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,540
Just watch what you say
so you don't end up as gossip,

156
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:04,880
and especially,

157
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:08,280
behave well so there are no rumors
about you and Hae Ra.

158
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:12,680
Sure, I'll keep that in mind.

159
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:29,100
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

160
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,400
Is this Na Hyun Hee?

161
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,840
Yes, how can I help you?

162
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:40,180
I'm Seo Hyun Jae
from the Cheongma Group Legal Team.

163
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:43,010
Hyun Hee,

164
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:46,650
could we talk a bit
about Manager Na Tae Hoon?

165
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:54,760
I'm not trying to interrogate
or pressure you.

166
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:58,460
If possible, I want to help you.

167
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,300
No. Don't call me.

168
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:03,870
Wait. Hyun Hee...

169
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:12,980
The phone is turned off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

170
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,210
After the beep...

171
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,480
Honey!

172
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:23,490
What on earth is this?

173
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,390
Isn't it obvious?

174
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:28,030
It's a contract.

175
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:30,130
What on earth did you do...

176
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,360
to get Chairman Kim
to approve a contract like this?

177
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,670
People will definitely talk.

178
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,300
This isn't a standard contract,

179
00:11:38,370 --> 00:11:39,800
it's special treatment.

180
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:41,170
Special treatment?

181
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:43,810
So what if we get
a little preferential treatment?

182
00:11:44,010 --> 00:11:46,310
Chairman Kim has always adored you.

183
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:49,780
And since he was so close
to your father,

184
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:52,620
shouldn't we be entitled
to this kind of special treatment?

185
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:54,750
Honey!

186
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:56,620
Don't get so worked up.

187
00:11:57,420 --> 00:12:00,720
This is all because he was moved
by the gift we gave him.

188
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,430
You're hiding something, aren't you?

189
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:04,900
Oh, please.

190
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,830
What could I be hiding?

191
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:11,240
Then why does Chairman Kim's wife
want me off the Fox Association?

192
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:14,310
I heard it from Ms. Yang
of Taekang Group today.

193
00:12:14,370 --> 00:12:16,940
She said I was expelled
from the Fox Association.

194
00:12:17,010 --> 00:12:18,310
Good riddance.

195
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,910
Use this opportunity to cut ties
with that useless...

196
00:12:21,010 --> 00:12:22,380
women's social club.

197
00:12:23,110 --> 00:12:24,520
Tell me the truth.

198
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,450
What on earth did you do
to Chairman Kim?

199
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:33,890
Fine, you should know the truth too.

200
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:38,830
Here, take a look.

201
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:43,900
What's this?

202
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,170
My gosh.

203
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,240
Honey...

204
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,670
Do you get it now?

205
00:12:49,570 --> 00:12:52,910
This is the true nature
of the man you respected so much.

206
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:55,180
Honey!

207
00:12:56,450 --> 00:12:57,480
Sure.

208
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,580
Yes, I understand.

209
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,250
You have so much on your plate,

210
00:13:03,690 --> 00:13:05,090
but it's not like we can help you.

211
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:07,890
It's fine.
You should head home already.

212
00:13:08,930 --> 00:13:09,990
Good luck, then.

213
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:19,200
And next time, speak up
if the workload is too heavy.

214
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,940
Say it's too much.

215
00:13:22,940 --> 00:13:24,480
Sure, I'll do that.

216
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:37,220
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

217
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:39,590
Hey, you're here.

218
00:13:39,990 --> 00:13:42,130
- Are you still working?
- No, I'm all done.

219
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:46,160
By the way,

220
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:49,530
is the CEO upset with me
about something?

221
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:51,570
Is my dad upset with you?

222
00:13:52,470 --> 00:13:53,540
I can't see why.

223
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,440
The new brand
is getting great traction,

224
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:56,670
so why would he be upset?

225
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:57,740
Really?

226
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:01,010
Why? Is something bothering you?

227
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:03,510
No.

228
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:07,720
Fathers with daughters
are all like that.

229
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:10,120
A son-in-law
who steals away your daughter is a thief.

230
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:14,790
You've been wearing your ring
a lot lately.

231
00:14:16,130 --> 00:14:17,360
You told me not to take it off.

232
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:19,960
My Seok Jin,

233
00:14:20,030 --> 00:14:21,870
you're being such a good boy lately.

234
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:23,330
Unbelievable.

235
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:27,100
Seok Jin. I forgot my pouch.

236
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,410
- Where is it?
- The office.

237
00:14:29,810 --> 00:14:31,040
Let's stop by for a second.

238
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,780
Okay.

239
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,020
Aren't you getting off work, Ms. Ko?

240
00:14:41,090 --> 00:14:42,090
No.

241
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:44,220
Work wasn't divided efficiently,

242
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,860
so I'm stuck working late.

243
00:14:47,690 --> 00:14:48,890
I'll go get my pouch.

244
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:59,070
Seok Jin, what should we eat today?

245
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,700
Keep up the good work, Ms. Ko.

246
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:02,340
Sure, have a good evening.

247
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:16,420
This is nice.

248
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:25,730
Ma'am, please join us.

249
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:27,160
This is the Pu'er tea
we just brought in.

250
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,570
The flavor profile is really deep.

251
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,340
Forget it. I'm good.

252
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,110
I'll have some later.

253
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:40,480
Oh, dear.

254
00:15:41,050 --> 00:15:42,310
Talk about holding a grudge.

255
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,180
She's going to be relentless
this time.

256
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,270
That's a photo of Dad.

257
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:03,830
Yes.

258
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:06,500
Why are you suddenly
dusting off Dad's picture like that?

259
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:12,210
Lately, I've been seeing
my husband a lot in my dreams.

260
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,880
Dad appears in your dreams?

261
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,480
Yes.

262
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:19,780
I wonder if something bad happened
up there in the afterlife,

263
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,650
because he keeps coming to me
in my dreams crying.

264
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,420
I wonder why.

265
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,990
Could something bad
really have happened to him?

266
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:33,100
My darling was
a really brave person.

267
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:35,300
So he rarely ever cried.

268
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,370
Tell me.
What kind of person was Dad?

269
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:43,810
My darling?

270
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:50,110
My darling loved me so much.

271
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,980
He also liked kimchi stew
with tuna...

272
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:55,350
much more than with pork.

273
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,390
What else?

274
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:01,460
Whenever he had an important event,

275
00:17:01,590 --> 00:17:03,990
he always carried
an ironed handkerchief.

276
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,960
- That's exactly like me.
- I know.

277
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,630
What else?

278
00:17:08,770 --> 00:17:09,770
More?

279
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,670
This is a bit embarrassing.

280
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:17,440
When he farted,
he would put his hand like this...

281
00:17:17,670 --> 00:17:19,880
and tell me to press right here.

282
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,980
Boop.

283
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:25,680
- Really?
- Yes, really.

284
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,720
Boop.

285
00:17:48,970 --> 00:17:50,840
Oh, hey. Thank you.

286
00:17:52,410 --> 00:17:55,980
I prepared something stronger
than what you usually drink.

287
00:17:57,210 --> 00:18:00,080
I was actually just needing
something strong.

288
00:18:11,230 --> 00:18:13,730
There's no need to get
your hands dirty. Let me do it.

289
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:35,050
Chairman Kim might come in.

290
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,120
Oh, right.

291
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:41,990
Director Joo, you can leave now.

292
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,160
Yes, sir.

293
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,080
Mr. Seok Jin.

294
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:00,810
Yes?

295
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:04,350
This belonged to my darling,
but I'll give it to you.

296
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:06,620
This was Dad's?

297
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:10,120
Yes. Since it was a gift from me,

298
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:13,090
he treasured it so much
that it's still like brand new.

299
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:15,990
He had something like this?

300
00:19:17,630 --> 00:19:18,900
Like this.

301
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:21,930
You might've forgotten
everything else,

302
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:24,200
but you still know how to tie a tie.

303
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:27,170
Of course I remember this.

304
00:19:30,310 --> 00:19:31,310
How does it look?

305
00:19:32,010 --> 00:19:33,180
Does your son look handsome?

306
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:35,910
You look sharp, Mr. Seok Jin.

307
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:41,520
But my darling
was much more handsome.

308
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:43,050
Oh, come on.

309
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,290
As if I don't know that.

310
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,360
Seok Jin.

311
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:52,230
Hey.

312
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,270
Your outfit is a bit off today.

313
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,230
Why? What's wrong with it?

314
00:19:58,170 --> 00:19:59,940
What is this, the '80s?

315
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,170
I think it looks fine.

316
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:05,010
Fine? Even my dad
wouldn't wear this.

317
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:14,280
This is the office.

318
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,590
Is that really
how you should greet someone?

319
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:44,750
Sir, did you have something to say?

320
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:46,420
Oh, right.

321
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:49,150
No, let's go.

322
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:03,770
This is the proposal to increase
the scholarship foundation budget.

323
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:04,970
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

324
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,570
Do I really have to review this
right now?

325
00:21:09,710 --> 00:21:11,410
You can get to it later, sir.

326
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,610
Yes, I'll do that.

327
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:17,450
You're dismissed.

328
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:19,420
Yes, sir.

329
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:23,150
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

330
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:30,230
(Chairman's Office)

331
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:46,010
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

332
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:05,130
(Year 2004)

333
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:08,130
- Young Hoon.
- Hey.

334
00:22:08,130 --> 00:22:10,770
- Here.
- Oh, right. Thanks.

335
00:22:12,770 --> 00:22:13,800
Hold on a second.

336
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:16,110
Is this a new tie?

337
00:22:16,370 --> 00:22:19,010
Yes, my wife got it for me
for our wedding anniversary.

338
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:21,280
Really? Looks expensive.

339
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:23,580
Hey, it's actually
from a department store.

340
00:22:23,650 --> 00:22:24,750
A silk tie.

341
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:26,950
Seriously. Are you showing off?

342
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:29,220
Seong Woo, let me try it on.

343
00:22:29,290 --> 00:22:31,460
- What? No way.
- Come on.

344
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,860
Is it because
it's from a department store?

345
00:22:32,860 --> 00:22:34,090
Let me try it on just once.

346
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,160
I said no.

347
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,100
Come on, it's a waste
if you don't wear it.

348
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,460
I'm even going to sleep in this.

349
00:22:39,530 --> 00:22:41,330
Seong Woo, come on!

350
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,700
Let me try it on just once,
you jerk.

351
00:22:43,770 --> 00:22:45,640
It's not because
I don't have ties of my own.

352
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:51,580
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

353
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:54,710
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

354
00:22:58,010 --> 00:22:59,120
This is just wrong.

355
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:00,620
What is?

356
00:23:01,050 --> 00:23:02,590
Your fashion sense is terrible.

357
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,520
Me?

358
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:07,860
What's wrong with my clothes?

359
00:23:08,730 --> 00:23:11,260
It looks like you need
a total makeover.

360
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:13,000
What makeover?

361
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:14,770
Seok Jin,

362
00:23:15,300 --> 00:23:17,900
you aren't going to Jae Seong's
launch event like that, are you?

363
00:23:18,770 --> 00:23:20,840
Why? Are you embarrassed
to be seen with me?

364
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:24,010
No, it's not that.

365
00:23:25,310 --> 00:23:27,980
My dad will be there,
and Chairman Min too.

366
00:23:28,310 --> 00:23:30,180
I'm trying to protect your image.

367
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:34,250
From now on, I'm going to
do better at supporting you.

368
00:23:35,450 --> 00:23:37,090
Is it that weird?

369
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:40,020
Let's go shopping together
after work.

370
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,760
Sure, whatever you say.

371
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:48,700
Are you okay?

372
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:51,870
I think the knife nicked me.

373
00:23:52,170 --> 00:23:53,300
Let me see.

374
00:23:56,470 --> 00:23:57,470
Oh no.

375
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:00,440
You should've been more careful.

376
00:24:00,910 --> 00:24:03,150
I told you to always be careful
when using a knife.

377
00:24:04,050 --> 00:24:05,350
You know I'm pretty strong.

378
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:07,550
I guess I overdid it a bit.

379
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:10,020
Why do you use that strength
so recklessly all the time?

380
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:11,720
You should use it
when it's actually needed.

381
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:12,760
Tell me about it.

382
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:15,160
The problem is
I have nowhere to use it.

383
00:24:15,330 --> 00:24:17,960
Must be nice having
so much extra energy.

384
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:20,030
Stay like this for a second.
We need to stop the bleeding first.

385
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:22,630
Boss, do you know something?

386
00:24:22,970 --> 00:24:23,970
Know what?

387
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:25,900
Sometimes when I look at you,

388
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:27,800
you remind me of my mom.

389
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:29,340
What?

390
00:24:30,140 --> 00:24:32,710
Getting scolded by you
and listening to your nagging?

391
00:24:33,610 --> 00:24:35,880
I feel like it's all coming
from my mom.

392
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:41,450
I'm back!

393
00:24:43,150 --> 00:24:44,250
Hey, son.

394
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:47,060
Mom, what are you and Uncle
doing right now?

395
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,060
What do you mean?

396
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,460
Are you and Uncle...

397
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,460
in love?

398
00:24:55,270 --> 00:24:56,630
What are you talking about?

399
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:59,570
Teun Teun, you have
quite the imagination.

400
00:24:59,970 --> 00:25:02,840
But the two of you
are holding hands tightly right now.

401
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:09,380
This doesn't mean we're dating.

402
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:11,450
Teun Teun, you have friends too.

403
00:25:11,620 --> 00:25:12,820
Friends that are girls.

404
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:14,150
Yes, I do.

405
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:16,950
Right. Then if that friend got hurt,

406
00:25:17,020 --> 00:25:18,560
would you just stand there
and watch?

407
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:21,120
- No. I'd help her.
- Exactly.

408
00:25:21,730 --> 00:25:24,430
Right now, your mom is just
helping a friend she works with.

409
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,560
I hurt my hand,
so she's helping me out.

410
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,700
We're not in love or anything.

411
00:25:30,670 --> 00:25:32,740
Exactly. That's just it.

412
00:25:33,470 --> 00:25:35,770
Oh, I see.

413
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:40,410
Put this on.

414
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:44,010
Seriously?
I thought you were going to help.

415
00:25:44,580 --> 00:25:45,920
I'll do it.

416
00:25:46,450 --> 00:25:48,490
Good boy, Teun Teun. Thank you.

417
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:57,130
Mr. Choi runs a butcher shop,

418
00:25:57,330 --> 00:26:00,300
so he's always betting with meat
at the card table.

419
00:26:01,260 --> 00:26:04,470
Still, I guess the meat
looks pretty good.

420
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:07,300
What good does that do?
It's completely useless to us.

421
00:26:07,870 --> 00:26:10,410
Whatever you cook
ends up straight...

422
00:26:11,110 --> 00:26:12,880
in the trash.

423
00:26:12,940 --> 00:26:14,780
Do you think I was like this
from the start?

424
00:26:15,150 --> 00:26:17,480
Eun Guk's mother
was such a good cook,

425
00:26:17,850 --> 00:26:19,820
so I got out of the habit
of cooking,

426
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:21,920
and now my food is inedible.

427
00:26:22,550 --> 00:26:25,120
That's not true.
You're really clueless.

428
00:26:25,620 --> 00:26:28,330
I was always an outcast
at lunchtime.

429
00:26:28,330 --> 00:26:30,660
- What?
- Whenever I opened my lunchbox,

430
00:26:30,830 --> 00:26:33,830
the other kids would back off
a few meters in every direction.

431
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:35,630
Do you know how lonely
I was in school...

432
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:38,400
because of
your terrible cooking skills?

433
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:39,700
All right, you punk.

434
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,570
Your mother has committed
a deadly sin.

435
00:26:43,270 --> 00:26:47,110
Anyway, what should we do
with this good meat?

436
00:26:49,380 --> 00:26:51,350
Wait. That's it!

437
00:26:51,950 --> 00:26:53,850
There's the landlady.

438
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:55,920
Teun Teun's mom?

439
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:57,490
Let's go.

440
00:26:57,550 --> 00:26:59,620
Let's take it to her
and share the meat.

441
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,260
Yes, rather than
throwing it all away,

442
00:27:02,630 --> 00:27:05,130
let's share it
and have a delicious meal.

443
00:27:05,130 --> 00:27:07,430
- Yes, let's go.
- Come on!

444
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:08,500
What else is there to life?

445
00:27:08,570 --> 00:27:09,900
Nothing beats good meat.

446
00:27:09,900 --> 00:27:11,270
That's right, the meat.

447
00:27:14,570 --> 00:27:18,510
Are things a bit uncomfortable
with the CEO lately?

448
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:23,350
If nothing else, Chairman Kim...

449
00:27:23,850 --> 00:27:27,080
was a junior colleague
my father cared for deeply.

450
00:27:28,450 --> 00:27:30,950
The fact that he disrespected
someone like that...

451
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:35,830
makes me feel like
he insulted my father in a way,

452
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:37,630
which I can't forgive.

453
00:27:39,630 --> 00:27:42,300
I can certainly see
why you'd feel that way.

454
00:27:42,700 --> 00:27:43,700
Exactly.

455
00:27:45,040 --> 00:27:47,740
So this time,
I'm not going to just let it slide.

456
00:27:49,170 --> 00:27:50,170
Of course.

457
00:27:52,040 --> 00:27:53,580
He never used to be like this,

458
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:56,110
but I think he has changed a lot.

459
00:27:58,380 --> 00:28:00,080
When we first met,

460
00:28:01,650 --> 00:28:04,320
he was such a sweet
and gentle person.

461
00:28:08,090 --> 00:28:12,530
I think the money and the position
have made him ruthless.

462
00:28:14,530 --> 00:28:17,270
He really has changed a lot.

463
00:28:29,110 --> 00:28:30,680
Everyone changes.

464
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,950
Is there anyone who doesn't?

465
00:28:33,980 --> 00:28:35,450
(Don't skimp on it
and apply generously.)

466
00:28:35,450 --> 00:28:36,920
(I'll gladly get you some more.)

467
00:28:40,490 --> 00:28:42,330
Don't skimp on it
and apply generously.

468
00:28:42,930 --> 00:28:44,090
I'll gladly get you some more.

469
00:28:46,030 --> 00:28:48,260
Has she lost her mind coming here?

470
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:50,070
Joo Ae Sook,
are you out of your mind?

471
00:28:54,270 --> 00:28:56,240
No wonder I had terrible luck today.

472
00:28:56,470 --> 00:28:58,580
You're like a curse, aren't you?

473
00:28:59,310 --> 00:29:00,580
Didn't I tell you not to come?

474
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:03,110
Are my words a joke?
Is your husband a joke to you?

475
00:29:04,650 --> 00:29:06,980
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

476
00:29:07,820 --> 00:29:10,490
But that money is all we have left.

477
00:29:11,150 --> 00:29:12,760
We have to pay off our debt with it.

478
00:29:12,790 --> 00:29:14,490
That's why your husband...

479
00:29:15,560 --> 00:29:17,760
is trying to double or triple it.

480
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:23,030
What can you do when even feelings
have an expiration date?

481
00:29:24,670 --> 00:29:26,300
The heart wears thin...

482
00:29:27,340 --> 00:29:29,070
until it spoils
and completely rots away.

483
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,440
I wonder...

484
00:29:33,740 --> 00:29:37,750
what kind of state
she's rotting in right now.

485
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:42,150
Thanks for sticking around so late.

486
00:29:42,590 --> 00:29:43,850
Being suddenly put
on the scholarship project...

487
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:44,920
has been hectic, right?

488
00:29:45,660 --> 00:29:48,690
Still, it's reassuring
to have you here.

489
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:52,230
I'm a bit hungry.
How about we grab some dinner?

490
00:29:52,560 --> 00:29:53,560
Sounds good.

491
00:29:54,330 --> 00:29:55,730
Hopefully not
at the cafeteria, though.

492
00:29:56,430 --> 00:29:57,430
Of course not.

493
00:29:57,900 --> 00:29:59,570
How about that udon tent
right outside today?

494
00:29:59,740 --> 00:30:00,740
What?

495
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:02,870
Seriously?

496
00:30:03,670 --> 00:30:04,670
Is that a no?

497
00:30:06,910 --> 00:30:08,880
Actually, I'm honored.

498
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:10,680
Let's go.

499
00:30:19,390 --> 00:30:20,920
You're Ko Eun Seol, right?

500
00:30:23,330 --> 00:30:24,330
Do I know you?

501
00:30:24,760 --> 00:30:26,930
I'm Na Hyun Hee,
Manager Na Tae Hoon's daughter.

502
00:30:30,830 --> 00:30:32,600
Manager Na Tae Hoon's...

503
00:30:33,970 --> 00:30:35,000
daughter?

504
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:37,540
Yes.

505
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:39,980
He was my dad,
and you're the reason he's dead.

506
00:31:12,010 --> 00:31:15,880
(A Trap Called Desire)

507
00:31:15,950 --> 00:31:17,250
Hae Ra, that's enough.

508
00:31:17,250 --> 00:31:18,550
I don't exist
just to make you look good.

509
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:20,320
Am I your arm candy?

510
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,880
You look a bit on edge.

511
00:31:21,950 --> 00:31:24,520
So you're not Cheongma's
prospective son-in-law,

512
00:31:24,650 --> 00:31:26,760
but just a candidate
for the position.

513
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:29,460
Isn't Mom the one
who actually owns Cheongma, not Dad?

514
00:31:29,530 --> 00:31:31,290
She must have been preparing
and waiting for this,

515
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:33,360
because she just poured it all out
on Ko Eun Seol.

516
00:31:33,430 --> 00:31:36,100
I always knew she would show up
at least once someday.

517
00:31:36,700 --> 00:31:39,000
How is An Guk Cheol
doing these days?

518
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:42,570
You must never tell Eun Seol. Never.

519
00:31:42,570 --> 00:31:44,040
Can I take a look at the profile?

520
00:31:44,110 --> 00:31:45,380
Just do me a solid, will you?

521
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:46,480
What the heck?

522
00:31:46,580 --> 00:31:49,180
Then Director Joo
is Eun Seol's biological mother?

523
00:31:49,780 --> 00:31:51,780
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
